🪜 Privilege Escalation
-----------------------
Checked what commands we could run as root without a password:
>$ sudo -l

Found
(ALL)NOPASSWD: /bin/cat .    
cat can be run as root with no password — a misconfiguration (cat shouldn’t be sudo-able, since it can read any file).

>$ sudo cat /root/root.txt

🚩ROOT Flag: 101101ddc16b0cdf65ba0b8a7af7afa5
